police. To explain the mark that remained visible across his neck for the next three months, he told others that he had been attacked during a mugging. Paul spotted Nielsen at the Golden Lion about a year after the incident but avoided speaking to him. In March 1982, four months after the attack on Paul Knobbs, Nielsen was drinking at the Salisbury on St Martin's Lane, London's pre-eminent gay bar, when he ran into 28-year-old John Howlett, whom Nielsen knew as John the Guardsman. The two had met at another pub a couple of months earlier, where John had boasted of being an ex-Grenadier Guardsman and they had chatted over drinks for a couple of hours. John had lived a troubled life. At the age of 13, he was kicked out of his family

