I wanted to touch and stroke him, but did not. I lay naked beside him, but only looked at the two bodies in the mirror. I just lay there and a great peace came over me. I felt that this was it, the meaning of life, death, everything. No fear, no pain, no guilt. I could only caress and fondle the image in the mirror. I never looked at him, no sex, just a feeling of oneness. The next morning, Nielsen dressed Stephen in some of his own clean clothes, placed his body in the living room wardrobe and went to work. One week later, on Thursday, February 3, downstairs tenant Jim Allcock noticed that one of the toilets on the ground floor of 23 Cranley Gardens was blocked. He attempted to unblock it

